These patches apply to https://github.com/bryangerlach/rdgen (GPL-3.0) and are GPL-3.0 like the rest of this repo.
UPSTREAM names the base commit. The host script copies this directory into the CT, where rdgen-setup applies it.
Patch 0009 is generated by tools/pullify.py and carries the trailer "Rdgen-Mechanical: pullify"; on a newer upstream it
is regenerated with pullify instead of being rebased.
0014 adds the hand-off of finished builds to CortenDesk's Client Downloads (`manage.py rdgen_publish`, used by
rdgen-publish). 0015 fills in the port, link, update URL and company fields from RDGEN_DEFAULT_*, explains every server field,
adds the settings reference and the as-you-type checks to the Other section, and fixes "Deny LAN discovery" and "Automatically close incoming sessions", which had no
effect upstream.
0016 gives Linux builds a Linux-safe app name (the packaging and the client's runtime both need one) and refuses names
that would replace a system command; pullify (0008/0009) also stages custom_.txt next to the renamed Linux program.
pullify (0008/0009) also keeps the Linux DRM job (an extra unattended-wayland .deb, RustDesk 1.5.0 on) from failing
builds: it puts back upstream's "Detect DRM support" step when nothing sets DRM_SUPPORTED, builds only where RustDesk
has --drm, skips the job in ARM-only builds and marks it continue-on-error; on a Linux runner of your own it runs
only with the repository variable RDGEN_LINUX_DRM=true. It also applies Flutter's dropdown patch only where the SDK
does not have it yet: a self-hosted runner keeps the SDK from the last build. And it sets rust-cache's cache-bin to
false on self-hosted runners, where its cleanup deleted rustup from $CARGO_HOME/bin after a successful job.
pullify (0008/0009) also writes the macOS custom_.txt into Contents/Resources (where RustDesk reads it; upstream used
Contents/MacOS, which signing treats as code) and drops upstream's rcodesign "Sign macOS app bundle" step in favour of
its own codesign step.
0017 adds the Recent builds page (/builds) and expiring share links (/share/<token>, no login); the console passes
only those two share paths to rdgen (RDGEN_SHARE_BASE, /etc/nginx/rustdesk-clients.conf).
0018 lets Recent builds delete a finished or failed build (files and share links at once, the row at the usual retention).
0019 explains the API server (with a warning for http:// host names), the connection type, where the permanent
password belongs (with a live note when it is unused) and what a build costs in Actions minutes.
0020 adds the form's "Mac builds" choice (input mac_arch); pullify builds the Mac matrix from it, lets repository
variables send Mac jobs to a self-hosted runner, and on a self-hosted Mac checks for Xcode and the tools
tools/runner-mac.sh installs instead of running brew install (steps gated on runner.environment).
0021 lets Linux and Windows jobs (and the helper jobs) go to self-hosted runners through repository variables,
adds the Linux build choices (linux_arch, linux_formats), and skips GitHub-image-only steps on self-hosted runners.
0022 records which runner ran each job of a build (one of GitHub's machines or a runner of yours), and the
form's cost note says where the last build of the chosen kind ran instead of always quoting GitHub's prices.
0023 refuses Windows app names that RustDesk 1.5.0 cannot install (anything but letters, digits and hyphens),
where "Accept and install" would silently do nothing.
0024 lets upstream's self-hosted update key (update_public_key, /api/generate only) through both checks: an
ed25519 public key in base64, else empty. Without the runner rule every build stopped at "Load Secrets"
("unknown keys"). With a key, upstream's allow_custom_update.py points the client's update check at
<downloadLink>/api/version/latest (a rustdesk-api endpoint; CortenDesk has none) and trusts metadata signed
with that key; pullify copies the script from the build repository instead of upstream master.
0025 makes the bootstrap's verify step (init, and the daily update) run the test suite as well, so an upstream
change that applies cleanly but breaks builds keeps the current version instead of reaching the CT.
0026 has the setup job refuse an app_version (a dispatch input outside the encrypted config, pasted into sed by
upstream's "Set custom app version" step) that is not x.y.z or x.y.z.w, and makes ghstub accept only the inputs
the workflows declare.
tools/rdgen-rebase.py moves the series to a newer upstream (rebase, 0009 regenerated, export, verify); the daily
workflow .github/workflows/rdgen-upstream.yml runs it.
patch-source (installed next to the patches in the CT, with github_known_hosts) lets a CT follow this directory
on a GitHub branch: rdgen-setup --patch-source <owner/repo>.
